+
+  WITHOUT THIS THE PROTOCOL SPLIT IS DECORATION. check_feature_support above
+  asks "does this device support the flow CLIENT", which is one bit -- it
+  cannot tell sFlow from NetFlow. Measured before this existed: a topology
+  asking for `protocol: netflow` against cEOS, which speaks only sFlow,
+  compiled CLEAN and rendered nothing. The device looked configured and
+  exported nothing, which is the exact failure this feature is meant to prevent
+  -- a lab that certifies green while its data plane is unobserved.
+
+  The split is not pedantry. Juniper divides by platform: sFlow on the switch,
+  inline IPFIX on the router. One flat `flow: True` capability would render
+  nothing on half the fleet and say so nowhere.
